              ************************
              Conformational Searching
              ************************

100 starting structures are used for all searches here.

(a) Execute Monte Carlo conformational search for ethanediol via
xCS100F etdiol

OUTPUT FILES:
sum contains a summary of the results. 
etdiol.cs.mol has the .mol file for each conformer.
etdiol.cs.out has the full output.
etdiol.cs.z has the Z-matrices for each conformer.
etdiol.cs.CSV is a comma-separated-file summarizing the key results. Display with gnumeric.

Time required for 1,2-ethanediol: 2 seconds on 2 GHz Intel  

The file mcsum has the results for the sum file, as executed at Yale.
To view all of the conformers on a PC, use WebLabViewer - enter
xWLMOL etdiol.cs

In WebLabViewer, use the Window/Hierarchy feature to separate the conformers into
individual structures. Otherwise,
if you wish to make an individual .mol file for each structure, enter
xCSMOL 
For individual Z-matrices, enter
xCSZ

(b) Execute MC conformational search including GB/SA solvation via
xCSGB100 etdiol
The file GBsum has the results for the sum file, as executed at Yale.

(c) Execute stochastic conformational search via
xSS100F etdiol

The file sssum has the results for the sum file, as executed at Yale.

OUTPUT FILES:
etdiol.ss.sum contains a summary of the results. 
etdiol.ss.mol has the .mol file for each conformer.
etdiol.ss.out has the full output.
etdiol.ss.z has the Z-matrices for each conformer.
The comma-separated-file is not written out.          

A kick radius of 2.0 A has been specified in the zmat file. This
would be too large for cyclic molecules, ca. 0.5 A is needed in
that case.
If there are no conformational search entries in the Z-matrix file,
the default values for stochastic search are:
NFIX =   0 RADIUS =     2.0000 PUSH =    0.1000 HWIDTH =    0.5000

The MC procedure finds the seven conformers. The stochastic
method finds six conformers - more starting structures can be
used, e.g., xSS200F etdiol

The etdiol.cs.mol file can be directly input to 
QikProp to obtain the properties predictions for each conformer:
xQPROP etdiol.cs.mol
(The xQPROP script must be in this directory or, for Windows, in the bat directory.)

The QikProp and BOSS results can then be combined with the script
xQPCON to obtain the conformationally averaged properties. Statistical
factors for degenerate conformers are not included. Sample
output is in conout.

------------------------------------------------------------------------

    September 19, 2000
    Conformational search has been enhanced. If MC conformational search is requested
    and no conformational search specifications are in the Z-matrix, the program will
    select the key non-ring bonds for torsional variation. With the xCS100 and xCS200
    scripts, the resulting conformers are in the plt.mol file. Execution of QikProp on
    plt.mol will then generate the QikProp predictions for each conformer. The
    conformational search and QikProp results can then be combined with the xQPCON
    script to obtain confromationally averaged properties for the gas-phase or
    aqueous-phase conformer distributions. E.g.,
    xCS100 celeco
    XQPROP plt.mol
    xQPCON
    will provide the results for celeco.z (celecoxib) in the drugs directory.

    The key point is that you can perform a reasonable conformational search now without
    providing any conformational search information in the Z-matrix. New scripts
    have also been added -

xCS100      - execute MC conformational search with 100 starting structures (usual)
xCS200      - execute MC conformational search with 200 starting structures (usual)
xCS500      - execute MC conformational search with 500 starting structures (usual)
xCS1K       - execute MC conformational search with 1000 starting structures (usual)
xCS100F     - execute MC CS with 100 starting structures - (with high resolution -
xCS200F     - execute MC CS with 200 starting structures - may get duplicate minima -
xCS500F     - execute MC CS with 500 starting structures - OK for small molecules)
xSS100      - execute stochastic conformational search with 100 starting structures 
xSS200      - execute stochastic conformational search with 200 starting structures 
xSS500      - execute stochastic conformational search with 500 starting structures 
xSS1K       - execute stochastic conformational search with 1000 starting structures 
xSS100F     - execute stochastic CS with 100 starting structures - with high resolution
xSS200F     - execute stochastic CS with 200 starting structures - with high resolution
xSS500F     - execute stochastic CS with 500 starting structures - with high resolution

xCSINFO     - utility: list energies of found conformers in csout
xCSMOL      - utility: create separate .mol files for each conformer; they can then
              be displayed individually with, e.g., RasMol

    x??100, x??200, etc. use less stringent comparison criterion for identifying
    duplicate conformers - appropriate for drug-like molecules.

    x??100F, x??200F, etc. provide higher resolution for small molecules; e.g., they
    will distinguish trans and gauche ethanol, x??100 and x??200 will not. All
    scripts will distinguish the four pentane conformers.

